<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44948" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spĕcŭlātōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		speculator, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to spies</i>
			or <i>scouts</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">navigia,</span>”
				<i>spy-boats</i>, <i>vessels of observation</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 4, 26</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also called speculatoriae naves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 30, 10, 14</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">35, 26, 9</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">36, 42, 8</span></i>; and
			caliga, <i>worn by spies</i> or <i>scouts</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 52</span></i>.— Hence,
				<i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spĕcŭlātōrĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> (Sc. navis.) <i>A spy-boat</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 22,
				19, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">22,
				36, 42</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> (Sc. caliga.) <i>A boot worn by spies</i>
			or <i>scouts</i>, <i><span class="en">Tert. Cor.
				Mil. 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
